history. Alternatively, checking the deployment\'s rollout history could show if there was a failed update. \n\nThe key is to find out why the \'currency\' pod is terminating. Possible causes include resource limits, failed health checks, or issues during deployment. Using `kubectl describe` on the deployment or pod could provide more insights. Also, checking the metrics again with a corrected query might help, but if that\'s not working, focusing on logs and deployment details is better.\n</think>\n\nget_traces  \nThe `get_traces` tool will retrieve distributed traces for the `currency` service, helping identify if there are errors, latency issues, or failed requests that might have led to the pod termination. Since the pod is in a `Terminating` state, traces could reveal anomalies in service interactions or internal errors causing the service to crash or be evicted. This will provide visibility into potential root causes like failed transactions, timeouts, or resource exhaustion. \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "get_traces", "arguments": {"service": "currency", "last_n_minutes": 5}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 633, 'prompt_tokens': 3340, 'total_tokens': 3973, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff3c-5ed8-7f02-af63-050c50e3b315-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3340, 'output_tokens': 633, 'total_tokens': 3973}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='2f34af8f-f2d1-4d70-ac9c-67177781fda2'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop a